# wip — monorepo-workspace-foundation
# Branch: feature/monorepo-workspace-foundation
# Started: 2026-03-20

#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Introduce visible workspace/package seams for v0.3.0 by making the repo a workspace root and adding package-level entrypoint facades before any large-scale physical code moves."
 ~#taste: "layering, clarity, containment"
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-20 00:07] observe — the repo currently has only src/{seed,runtime,testing} plus root scripts; package ownership is implied rather than encoded.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:07] observe — scripts and extensions reference src/seed, src/runtime, and scripts/lsp directly, so a full move would create broad churn.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:07] decide — first land workspace scaffolding and package facades so later relocation can happen incrementally.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:07] taste — prefer one compatibility layer per package over a half-moved tree with unstable imports.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:11] decide — scope the initial workspace to packages/* plus extensions/vscode-spw, because IntelliJ is not an npm workspace surface.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:11] revise — root exports now point at package facades for seed/runtime while scripts remain on current paths.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:11] decide — CLI gets a real facade over scripts/spw-cli, while LSP stays a truthful scaffold constant until executable extraction is ready.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:14] observe — root runtime tests still fail on Substrate.bind expectations, which appears pre-existing and outside this workspace scaffold slice.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:15] observe — direct smoke imports for all new package facades succeed, so the new seams are loadable even though root build/test still carry unrelated pre-existing failures.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:21] revise — switched root script and analyzer imports from direct src/seed references to @spw/seed / @spw/cli where the facade already exists.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:21] observe — spw help, spwq, spw-format, spw-mount, and spw-syntax-validate all execute successfully through the package aliases.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:35] observe — @spw/cli still reaches back into scripts/spw-cli/* and @spw/lsp is only a constant, so the package seams are visible but not yet operationally primary.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:35] observe — editor integrations still default to scripts/lsp/stdio-server.ts, which means package ownership is not the default launch path anywhere outside npm aliases.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:35] decide — move CLI and LSP launch ownership into packages/* and leave scripts/* as compatibility wrappers until the deeper implementation move lands.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:35] taste — package seams should be truthful enough that a new contributor finds packages/* first and scripts/* second.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:53] revise — CLI command parsing, query execution, and package entry now live in packages/spw-cli/src/*, while scripts/spw-cli/* collapse to compatibility re-exports.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:53] revise — the LSP bridge now prefers packages/spw-lsp/src/stdio-server.ts, preserves scripts/lsp/stdio-server.ts as a fallback, and updates editor defaults toward the package path.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:53] observe — npm run spw, scripts/spw.ts, spwq, and direct @spw/lsp target resolution all work through the new package-owned entrypoints.
 >>[2026-03-20 00:53] observe — lsp smoke ends at the same 20 passed / 2 failed references-timeout profile on both package and legacy server paths, so the remaining failures appear pre-existing rather than introduced by this extraction.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:06] fix — build blockers are branded RegisterId drift in interpreter/resonance and a missing Substrate.bind implementation causing 4 runtime test failures.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:06] decide — clear the runtime blockers first so module relocation can be verified against a truthful build/test baseline rather than against already-broken state.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:06] decide — after the blocker fix, move the LSP implementation modules behind packages/spw-lsp instead of stopping at entrypoint wrappers.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:11] revise — brand template tags now accept interpolations, so the runtime fix can keep using $register ergonomics even for synthesized or user-provided keys.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:11] fix — npm run build and npm run test:run now pass after restoring Substrate.bind and tightening branded register flows in interpreter, resonance, and register-bank code.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:44] revise — copied the LSP implementation modules into packages/spw-lsp/src/*, rewired the package server to those local modules, and collapsed scripts/lsp/* back down to compatibility wrappers.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:44] revise — branded ID factories are now symmetric across register/frame/domain/layer, with template-tag support preserved while keeping direct constructor-style calls available.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:44] observe — npm run build, npm run test:run, npm run lsp:smoke, and node --import tsx scripts/spw.ts help all pass against the package-owned LSP module tree.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:58] revise — copied the runtime interpreter/pipeline/state implementation tree into packages/spw-runtime/src/* and rewired those package modules to depend on @spw/seed plus local runtime internals.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:58] revise — collapsed src/runtime/* implementation files to compatibility wrappers so existing tests and references keep pointing at the familiar surface while the package becomes the real owner.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:58] revise — widened the @spw/seed root export surface and added explicit Vitest alias wiring so package-path imports resolve consistently in both typecheck and test execution.
 >>[2026-03-20 01:58] observe — npm run build, npm run test:run, npm run lsp:smoke, and node --import tsx scripts/spw.ts help all pass with runtime execution now owned by packages/spw-runtime.
}

